# The man page is generated by upstream's xtask from the same block
# documentation the website renders, which is 122 tbl tables of option keys,
# value descriptions and defaults. Several cells hold prose longer than the
# column, so groff reports "cannot adjust line" (193) and "cannot break line"
# (31) while setting them.
#
# These are typography complaints about upstream's content, not defects in the
# page. The alternative was worse and was what the first build shipped: without
# the "'\" t" preprocessor line that debian/rules now prepends, tbl never ran
# and every table rendered as its own source -- literal `T{ Key T}@T{ Values
# T}` runs in the middle of the text. Compared against a rendered page before
# overriding this.
i3status-rust: groff-message
